      "content": "I know you'd love to just get the answer, but working through it together will make sure you ace this in the exam! 🧭\n\nTo find the gradient of a line, we use a handy little saying: **\"Rise over Run\"** (how far up/down you go divided by how far across you go). \n\nBefore we plug anything in, can you write down the coordinates of points $A$ and $B$ from the question?"
