      "content": "You've got the correct coordinates! \n\nRemember our mnemonic **Rise over Run**: $\\text{Gradient} = \\frac{\\text{Change in } y}{\\text{Change in } x} = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}$.\n\nUsing $A(-5; -3)$ as point 1 and $B(4; 12)$ as point 2, what do you get when you calculate the top part: $y_2 - y_1$?"
